  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we compute the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+(5+1)^{-2}=\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+{6}^{-2}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that ${6}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{36}.$ So, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+{6}^{-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{36}\\times 2+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{36}\\times \\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 2}{36\\times 1}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{10}{36}+\\frac{1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{10+1}{36} & = \\\\ \\frac{11}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
